// Deliberately broken grammar file. Do NOT copy its structure, and do NOT
// try to fix it: it exists to exercise the failure paths, and the test
// suite plus the default ignore set depend on it staying invalid.
//
// What is wrong with it (one defect per marker below): a negative
// schema version, a grammar value that is not a string, and an unknown
// top-level key. Loading this file normally ends in a structured grammar
// error instead of a traceback.
//
// Why it is still here: ``flags.ignore`` contains ``err.json5`` by
// default, so everyday runs skip it silently. To see the failure it
// produces, pass your own ``--ignore`` value (any explicit value replaces
// the default set, so this file gets loaded) or clear the set
// programmatically. That round-trip -- broken file in, structured error
// out -- is the intended first example of how ``--ignore`` shapes
// grammar discovery.
{
  "cmd-router": {
    // Invalid schema version
    "schema-version": -1,
    "grammar": {
      // Invalid grammar map
      "gamemode": 5,
    },
    // Unknown key
    "unknown": "key"
  },
}